    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'll keep an eye on how it feels. do you have any advice on how to stay motivated when it starts getting tough? like, what's the mental game for sticking to a program when you're just tired and don't want to go to the gym?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Staying motivated can be a challenge. Here are some tips to help you:\n\n- Set specific, achievable goals for yourself (e.g., complete a certain number of workouts, reach a new personal best)\n- Create a routine and stick to it, even on weekends and days off\n- Find a workout buddy or accountability partner to help keep you motivated\n- Reward yourself after reaching milestones or completing a challenging workout\n- Remind yourself of your \"why\" - what drove you to start lifting in the first place? Focus on the progress and positive outcomes, not just the physical aspect\n- Keep track of your progress, whether it's through a workout journal, photos, or measurements. This can help you see the changes in your body and stay motivated",
      "source": "target",
